{"objective":"Close the first agent-feedback wave on the MCP surface and unify the CLI entrypoint. Four GitHub issues filed by agents consuming eka-mcp were verified against source and translated into work items; one item unifies the `eka mcp` / `eka mcp serve` command family into an information+interactive-installer entrypoint and a silent protocol-only server command that per-agent configurations can standardize on; one item restores error fidelity at the MCP tool boundary so refusals carry their full diagnostic reports instead of count-only summaries.","scope":"Six work items, sequenced by priority:\n1. bug:mcp-new-false-refusal - make the eka_new refusal discriminate its three causes, define the required-field contract once (schema + enforcement derived from it), add refusal-time diagnostics (GitHub issue #28).\n2. sto:mcp-read-content-controls - expose noContent on the get/domain MCP tools at parity with the CLI (GitHub issue #26).\n3. sto:mcp-transition-transparency - surface legalTransitions in publish/scaffold/draft-inspection results from the conformance state tables (GitHub issue #27).\n4. sto:mcp-authoring-round-trips - add a sanctioned draft mutation tool and expose batch publish on the MCP boundary (GitHub issue #25).\n5. sto:mcp-error-fidelity - unwrap structured validation errors at the MCP boundary so refusals embed full reports; surface transition warning/confirmation affordances.\n6. sto:mcp-entrypoint-ux - bare `eka mcp` becomes info + interactive installer (agent picker, global-vs-repo scope picker); `eka mcp serve` becomes the silent server command referenced by per-agent configs.\n\nCross-cutting acceptance: each GitHub issue receives a review-findings comment and is closed only after its fix ships in a release.","outOfScope":"- Flipping domain listings to identity-only by default (breaking change; deferred behind opt-in noContent until a major version).\n- Merging scaffold+publish into a single authoring call (declined: collapses two lifecycle steps and weakens the draft review gate).\n- Chasing a unicode-parsing fix for the intermittent eka_new refusal (Go's JSON decoder does not reject unicode; root cause lies in refusal-message conflation and upstream byte delivery).\n- Re-running validation on refusal inside the MCP layer to restore error detail (rejected: double cost, TOCTOU drift, bespoke handling per refusal class - structured errors are unwrapped instead).\n- Any new MCP tools beyond those named in the scoped work items."}